---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Trip Planner"
  description="Six-day itinerary for driving Arizona's haunted Route 66, from Holbrook to Oatman."
>

  <div class="container">

    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>PLAN YOUR ROAD TRIP</h1>
      <p>Six days on Arizona's Haunted Route 66</p>
    </header>

    <section class="trip-intro">
      <p>
        This itinerary follows the route taken by our panelists during their six-day paranormal
        investigation of Arizona's Route 66. We drove every mile, visited every haunted location,
        and slept in some of the most ghost-prone lodgings on the Mother Road.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the full account of that journey, see Debe Branning's
        <em>Arizona's Haunted Route 66</em>, published by Haunted America.
      </p>
      <div class="trip-stats">
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat-num">6</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Days</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat-num">13</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Haunted Stops</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <span class="stat-num">~400</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Miles</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Day 1 ── -->
    <section class="day" id="day-1">
      <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 1</span>
        <h2>HOLBROOK</h2>
        <p class="day-sub">The Cursed Bones and the Reluctant Hanging</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day-body">
        <div class="stops">
          <a href="/stories/petrified-forest/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">01</span>
            <div>
              <strong>The Curse of the Petrified Forest</strong>
              <span>Petrified Forest National Park</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/stories/navajo-county-courthouse/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">02</span>
            <div>
              <strong>George Smiley's Ghost</strong>
              <span>Navajo County Courthouse, Holbrook</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="day-details">
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>DRIVE TIME</h4>
            <p>Petrified Forest to Holbrook: ~30 miles, 35 min on Route 66</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>OVERNIGHT</h4>
            <p class="tbd">Lodging recommendation coming soon</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>LOCAL TIP</h4>
            <p class="tbd">Side stories and practical tips coming soon</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Day 2 ── -->
    <section class="day" id="day-2">
      <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 2</span>
        <h2>WINSLOW TO FLAGSTAFF</h2>
        <p class="day-sub">The Fred Harvey Ghost and the Cursed Canyon</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day-body">
        <div class="stops">
          <a href="/stories/la-posada-hotel/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">03</span>
            <div>
              <strong>La Posada's Mysterious Guests</strong>
              <span>La Posada Hotel, Winslow</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/stories/two-guns/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">04</span>
            <div>
              <strong>The Apache Death Cave &amp; Cursed Two Guns</strong>
              <span>Canyon Diablo, I-40 Exit 230</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="day-details">
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>DRIVE TIME</h4>
            <p>Holbrook to Winslow: ~33 miles, 35 min &bull; Winslow to Two Guns: ~35 miles, 40 min &bull; Two Guns to Flagstaff: ~45 miles, 50 min</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>OVERNIGHT</h4>
            <p class="tbd">Lodging recommendation coming soon</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>WHILE IN WINSLOW</h4>
            <p>Don't miss the Standing on a Corner park — the famous Eagles lyric made real in bronze and murals on Second Street, one block from La Posada.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Day 3 ── -->
    <section class="day" id="day-3">
      <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 3</span>
        <h2>FLAGSTAFF</h2>
        <p class="day-sub">Three Haunted Stops in Arizona's Most Haunted City</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day-body">
        <div class="stops">
          <a href="/stories/hotel-monte-vista/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">05</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Hotel Monte Vista's Celebrity Ghosts</strong>
              <span>100 N San Francisco St, Flagstaff</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/stories/weatherford-hotel/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">06</span>
            <div>
              <strong>The Weatherford's Eternal Honeymooners</strong>
              <span>23 N Leroux St, Flagstaff</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/stories/museum-club/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">07</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Don and Thorna's Museum Club</strong>
              <span>3404 E Route 66, Flagstaff</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="day-details">
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>FLAGSTAFF GHOST TOUR</h4>
            <p>The Flagstaff Visitor Center (itself reportedly haunted) offers a free self-guided ghost tour brochure covering downtown. Pick one up and walk the area between the Monte Vista and Weatherford — it's two blocks apart.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>OVERNIGHT</h4>
            <p class="tbd">Lodging recommendation coming soon — consider staying at the Monte Vista or Weatherford themselves if you dare.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>MUSEUM CLUB NOTE</h4>
            <p>The Museum Club is primarily a live music venue. Check their calendar before visiting — it's best experienced when there's a show.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Day 4 ── -->
    <section class="day" id="day-4">
      <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 4</span>
        <h2>WILLIAMS &amp; PEACH SPRINGS</h2>
        <p class="day-sub">The Murdered Madam and the Disturbed Dead</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day-body">
        <div class="stops">
          <a href="/stories/red-garter-inn/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">08</span>
            <div>
              <strong>The Red Garter Inn's Murdered Madam</strong>
              <span>137 W Railroad Ave, Williams</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/stories/grand-canyon-caverns/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">09</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Grand Canyon Caverns' Restless Spirits</strong>
              <span>Mile 115, Route 66, Peach Springs</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="day-details">
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>DRIVE TIME</h4>
            <p>Flagstaff to Williams: ~32 miles, 35 min &bull; Williams to Grand Canyon Caverns: ~65 miles, 1 hr 15 min on Route 66</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>OVERNIGHT</h4>
            <p class="tbd">Lodging recommendation coming soon — the Caverns offers underground hotel rooms if you're brave enough.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>WILLIAMS DETOUR</h4>
            <p>Williams is the southern gateway to the Grand Canyon (60 miles north). If your schedule allows, a morning trip to the South Rim before heading west is well worth the detour.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Day 5 ── -->
    <section class="day" id="day-5">
      <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 5</span>
        <h2>HACKBERRY &amp; KINGMAN</h2>
        <p class="day-sub">The Desert Prospector and the Divided Hotel</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day-body">
        <div class="stops">
          <a href="/stories/hackberry-mine/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">12</span>
            <div>
              <strong>The Hackberry Mine Murders</strong>
              <span>Hackberry, AZ</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/stories/hotel-brunswick/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">10</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Hotel Brunswick's Love Triangle</strong>
              <span>105 E Andy Devine Ave, Kingman</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="day-details">
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>DRIVE TIME</h4>
            <p>Peach Springs to Hackberry: ~65 miles via Route 66 &bull; Hackberry to Kingman: ~35 miles, 40 min</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>OVERNIGHT</h4>
            <p class="tbd">Lodging recommendation coming soon</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>KINGMAN NOTE</h4>
            <p>Kingman is the largest city on Arizona's Route 66 and a good base for the western portion of the trip. Route 66 through downtown Kingman (Andy Devine Avenue) has a well-preserved stretch worth walking on foot.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Day 6 ── -->
    <section class="day" id="day-6">
      <div class="day-header">
        <span class="day-badge">DAY 6</span>
        <h2>OATMAN</h2>
        <p class="day-sub">Hollywood Ghosts, Wild Burros, and the End of the Road</p>
      </div>
      <div class="day-body">
        <div class="stops">
          <a href="/stories/oatman-hotel/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">11</span>
            <div>
              <strong>The Oatman Hotel's Hollywood Ghosts</strong>
              <span>181 Main St, Oatman, AZ</span>
            </div>
          </a>
          <a href="/stories/phantom-hitchhikers/" class="stop-link">
            <span class="stop-num">13</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Route 66's Phantom Hitchhikers</strong>
              <span>The entire Arizona stretch</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        </div>
        <div class="day-details">
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>DRIVE TIME</h4>
            <p>Kingman to Oatman: ~28 miles but allow 45–60 min — the road through the Black Mountains is twisty and spectacular.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>THE GOLD ROAD</h4>
            <p>The drive from Kingman to Oatman on the original Route 66 through Sitgreaves Pass is one of the most dramatic stretches of road in Arizona. Don't rush it. Pull over at the top for the view.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="detail-block">
            <h4>OATMAN TIPS</h4>
            <p>The wild burros own the town and they know it. Bring carrots — sold at shops in town. The daily staged gunfights happen on Main Street at set times. Check the schedule when you arrive.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── Practical Info ── -->
    <section class="practical">
      <h2>PRACTICAL INFORMATION</h2>
      <div class="practical-grid">
        <div class="practical-card">
          <h3>BEST TIME TO VISIT</h3>
          <p class="tbd">Recommendations coming soon</p>
        </div>
        <div class="practical-card">
          <h3>WHAT TO BRING</h3>
          <p class="tbd">Packing list and gear recommendations coming soon</p>
        </div>
        <div class="practical-card">
          <h3>ROAD CONDITIONS</h3>
          <p class="tbd">Route 66 road condition notes coming soon</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding: var(--space-lg) 0 var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }
  .page-header h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 3.5rem); margin: 0 0 0.3rem; }
  .page-header p  { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-style: italic; margin: 0; }

  /* ── Intro ── */
  .trip-intro {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }
  .trip-intro p { color: var(--color-text-muted); }

  .trip-stats {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .stat-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 3rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-accent-amber);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .stat-label {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* ── Day sections ── */
  .day {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .day:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }

  .day-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .day-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    color: var(--color-accent-amber);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-accent-amber);
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    align-self: flex-start;
  }

  .day-header h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.8rem);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .day-sub {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .day-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-lg);
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* ── Stop links ── */
  .stops {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .stop-link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    padding: var(--space-sm);
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color 0.2s;
  }
  .stop-link:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-accent-amber);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .stop-num {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--color-accent-amber);
    line-height: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    min-width: 2rem;
  }

  .stop-link div {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .stop-link strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .stop-link span {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  /* ── Day details ── */
  .day-details {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .detail-block h4 {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    color: var(--color-accent-green);
    margin: 0 0 0.3rem;
  }

  .detail-block p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .tbd {
    font-style: italic;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  /* ── Practical ── */
  .practical {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .practical h2 {
    font-size: 1.8rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .practical-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .practical-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: var(--space-md);
  }
  .practical-card h3 {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-sm);
  }
  .practical-card p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ── Responsive ── */
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .day-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .practical-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
